CORE
main.c
--no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --index-chain --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^index chain: [1-9][0-9]* of
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The read of x is decoded by index over the writes it can see: index 0 (the
value before the first write), the writes of other threads, and the reading
thread's own earlier writes. Verified by mutation: leaving the reading thread's
own earlier writes out of that set leaves the read unconstrained when the chain
holds main's write, and this test then reports VERIFICATION FAILED.
